# clutch-deploy — the TESTNET's env file. Copy to .env.testnet on the host and fill it in; it is gitignored.
#
# ONE FILE PER NETWORK (since 2026-10-07):
#   .env.testnet   the stage stack, project clutch-stage: its chain, Hub API, explorer, treasury, and
#                  the monitoring (Prometheus, Grafana, Seq, Alertmanager) that watches both networks.
#                  Also local dev (project clutch-dev). Template: this file.
#   .env.mainnet   ALL of mainnet: validators, Hub API, explorer (project clutch-main) and the treasury
#                  (project clutch-main-treasury). Template: .env.mainnet.example.
# Every compose command passes its file: `docker compose -p clutch-stage --env-file .env.testnet ...`.
# Without --env-file compose reads a file named .env, which no longer exists on the host. Every secret
# in .env.mainnet must differ from the ones here.
#
# Compose substitutes these into the services that name them, and nothing else: no service is
# handed this whole file. Plain settings that are the same on every host live in config/ instead
# (config/api, config/explorer and config/node for the testnet; the *-mainnet folders for mainnet).

# =============================================================================================
# 1. Monitoring and logging (they run in the stage project and serve both networks)
# =============================================================================================

# Seq. The ingestion key goes to every testnet Rust service as APP_SEQ_API_KEY; .env.mainnet carries
# the same key for the mainnet services. Create it in the Seq UI, then paste it here. The admin pair applies only on first run with an empty volume.
SEQ_API_KEY=seq-ingestion-api-key
SEQ_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
SEQ_ADMIN_PASSWORD=seq-admin-password

# Grafana's admin password. Required; "Provision treasury secrets" generates it.
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-grafana-admin

# Where alerts go. Readiness item D3/D4: fifteen Prometheus rules exist and none of them reaches a
# human without these.
#
#   1. Message @BotFather on Telegram, /newbot, copy the token it gives you.
#   2. Send your new bot any message, then open
#      https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates and read chat.id from the response.
#      Negative for a group. The bot cannot message you until you have written to it first.
#
# deploy-stage.sh writes the token to config/monitoring/alertmanager/telegram-token and renders
# alertmanager.yml from the .tpl with the chat id substituted. Both are gitignored. Unset, the
# deploy renders placeholders, Alertmanager starts, and delivery fails visibly in its own log —
# which is honest, and is not the item being closed.
#
# The item closes when a forced failure has actually arrived: stop treasury-service for four
# minutes and confirm TreasuryServiceDown reaches you.
ALERT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
ALERT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# =============================================================================================
# 2. Testnet (stage) apps
# =============================================================================================

# Signs the tokens the testnet Hub API issues, which the testnet orchestrator trusts. The hub refuses
# to start on an empty, placeholder or short value; "Provision treasury secrets" generates it.
JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-key-here

# CORS for the testnet Hub API and the testnet deposit API (comma-separated). Include the demo origin.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173,https://app-stage.clutchprotocol.io

# The testnet explorer. Its other settings (the node it reads, wiping its index on start) are in
# config/explorer/default.toml. inspect-stage.sh reads the user and database names too.
EXPLORER_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=*
EXPLORER_POSTGRES_DB=clutch_explorer
EXPLORER_POSTGRES_USER=postgres
EXPLORER_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres

# =============================================================================================
# 3. Testnet treasury
# =============================================================================================
# GENERATED on the host by "Provision treasury secrets" (scripts/provision-treasury-secrets.sh),
# which never overwrites. Leave them out of a hand-written file:
#   TREASURY_POSTGRES_PASSWORD, ORCHESTRATOR_POSTGRES_PASSWORD, MINT_AUTHORITY_SECRET,
#   SIGNER_TOKEN, TREASURY_INITIATOR_TOKEN, TREASURY_APPROVER_TOKEN, TREASURY_READONLY_TOKEN,
#   DEPOSIT_MNEMONIC, DEPOSIT_ACCOUNT_XPUB, PAYOUT_FLOAT_ADDRESS,
#   TRONGRID_URL and USDT_CONTRACT (pinned to Nile), TRONGRID_API_KEY (from the repo secret),
#   and JWT_SECRET and GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD above.
# YOURS, by hand:
#   CUSTODY_TRON_ADDRESS=   a Nile wallet you control, where swept USDT lands; provisioning aborts without it
#   BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=      openssl rand -base64 48; keep a copy off the host. The nightly backup aborts without it.
#   BACKUP_REMOTE=          optional rclone destination for the dumps; without it they stay on this disk
# Limits and intervals have defaults in docker-compose.treasury.yml; set one here only to change it
# (set-mint-caps.yml writes the two mint caps). check-cap-invariants.sh must pass after any change.

# The GasFree rail: USDT sweeps and payouts with no TRX, the relay's fee paid in USDT. OFF while
# GASFREE_NETWORK is unset. See clutch-treasury's docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-gasfree-transfer-rail-design.md
# §6, and docs/ON-CALL.md "The GasFree rail". Values below are the testnet's (Nile).
#
# Keep every line set for as long as any user has a GasFree address, or the GasFree float holds USDT,
# even after going back to TRANSFER_RAIL=trx. Put the key and the secret in unquoted, and never into a
# chat, a commit or a log.
# Keep each comment on its own line: check-cap-invariants.sh reads a value to the end of its line.
# On stage, "Set GasFree settings (stage)" writes these lines, all but the key and the secret.
#
# TRANSFER_RAIL=gasfree
# GASFREE_NETWORK=nile
# GASFREE_API_URL=https://open-test.gasfree.io/nile
# Set GASFREE_API_KEY and GASFREE_API_SECRET only together with GASFREE_NETWORK: tron-signer turns
# GasFree on by the key alone and then refuses to start without the network, so
# check-cap-invariants.sh stops the stage deploy while the key is set and the network is not.
# GASFREE_API_KEY=
# GASFREE_API_SECRET=
# The relay's own address; PROBE=gasfree prints the provider list.
# GASFREE_SERVICE_PROVIDER=TKtWbdzEq5ss9vTS9kwRhBp5mXmBfBns3E
# Above the live fees (1.00 and 0.30 on Nile). Users are charged these in full, and the app says so. The
# relay may charge less; the difference is not refunded: it stays in the reserve as backing.
# GASFREE_ACTIVATE_FEE_MAX_USDT=1500000
# GASFREE_TRANSFER_FEE_MAX_USDT=500000
# After the fee, a deposit below this mints nothing and waits for a human.
# MIN_DEPOSIT_USDT=1000000
# GasFree's reviewed code; PROBE=gasfree prints the live values.
# GASFREE_EXPECTED_IMPLEMENTATION=b8eda40b467b45af107f198e94cc2fa1378adf50
# GASFREE_EXPECTED_CONTROLLER_IMPLEMENTATION=2ec1c0ada96ac9c3d6aab8e0c6e18194ed72c441
# A sweep goes to the float while it holds less than this, and to custody after that. $1,000,000 is
# never reached on Nile, so every sweep goes to the float and custody stays empty: "one wallet", as on
# mainnet since 2026-10-05. It must stay at least the largest payout plus its relay fee.
# PAYOUT_FLOAT_TARGET_USDT=1000000000000

# =============================================================================================
# 4. Local dev only (docker-compose.dev.yml): for npm installs behind a proxy or a mirror
# =============================================================================================
# NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY=https://registry.npmjs.org/
# HTTP_PROXY=
# HTTPS_PROXY=
# NO_PROXY=
